huge|very-large|ADJECTIVE|Very large|Far above the usual size or quantity.|rất lớn, khổng lồ|A huge pile of letters covered the receptionist's desk.|Một đống thư rất lớn phủ kín bàn của nhân viên lễ tân.|Used before a noun or after a linking verb; can describe size or amount.|huge
baseball|bat-and-ball-sport|NOUN|Bat-and-ball team sport|A sport in which players hit a ball with a bat and run between bases.|bóng chày|We listened to a baseball match on the radio during the drive.|Chúng tôi nghe một trận bóng chày trên radio trong lúc đi xe.|Uncountable when naming the sport; a baseball game is countable.|baseball
galaxy|star-system|NOUN|Vast system of stars|A vast group of stars and other matter held together by gravity.|thiên hà|Astronomers photographed a distant galaxy through the telescope.|Các nhà thiên văn chụp ảnh một thiên hà xa xôi qua kính thiên văn.|Countable; the Milky Way is the galaxy that contains our solar system.|galaxy
react|respond|VERB|Respond to a stimulus|To act or change in response to something that happens.|phản ứng|The dog reacted to the whistle by lifting its ears.|Con chó phản ứng với tiếng còi bằng cách vểnh tai lên.|React to something; describes a response rather than the initial action.|react
jacket|short-coat|NOUN|Short outer garment|An outer garment covering the upper body, usually reaching around the waist or hips.|áo khoác ngắn|He zipped his jacket before stepping onto the windy platform.|Anh ấy kéo khóa áo khoác trước khi bước ra sân ga lộng gió.|Countable; styles and materials vary. This Sense concerns clothing.|jacket
supper|evening-meal|NOUN|Evening meal|A meal eaten towards the end of the day.|bữa tối|We shared soup and fresh bread for supper.|Chúng tôi cùng ăn súp và bánh mì mới cho bữa tối.|Often uncountable in have supper or for supper; regional meal names vary.|supper
trash|discarded-waste|NOUN|Discarded waste|Things thrown away because they are no longer wanted or useful.|rác, đồ bị bỏ đi|Volunteers collected the trash left beside the picnic tables.|Các tình nguyện viên nhặt rác bị bỏ lại cạnh những bàn ăn dã ngoại.|Usually uncountable; especially American English, often rubbish in British English.|trash
cow|female-cattle|NOUN|Adult female cattle|An adult female of the cattle species.|bò cái trưởng thành|The farmer led the cow into the shed before the storm.|Người nông dân dắt con bò cái vào chuồng trước cơn bão.|Countable; cow specifically identifies the female animal in this Sense.|cow
vivid|bright-colour|ADJECTIVE|Bright and visually striking|Having strong, clear colours that attract attention.|rực rỡ, sáng rõ về màu sắc|Vivid orange flowers lined the narrow garden path.|Những bông hoa màu cam rực rỡ mọc dọc lối đi hẹp trong vườn.|Used here for colours and visual appearance, not the separate memory use.|vivid
equipment|purpose-tools|NOUN|Tools for an activity|The tools and devices needed to carry out a particular activity.|thiết bị, dụng cụ phục vụ một hoạt động|The rescue team checked its diving equipment before departure.|Đội cứu hộ kiểm tra thiết bị lặn của mình trước khi khởi hành.|Uncountable; say a piece of equipment, not an equipment or equipments.|equipment
replace|substitute|VERB|Put another in its place|To remove one thing from use and put another in its place.|thay thế|They replaced the cracked window with stronger glass.|Họ thay cửa kính bị nứt bằng kính chắc hơn.|Replace A with B; A is what is removed, B is the substitute.|replace
cent|currency-unit|NOUN|Hundredth of a currency unit|A monetary unit worth one hundredth of a dollar, euro, or certain other currencies.|xu, đơn vị bằng một phần trăm đô la hoặc euro|The price rose by five cents overnight.|Giá tăng năm xu chỉ sau một đêm.|Countable; specify the currency when the monetary system is unclear.|cent
sensor|detecting-device|NOUN|Device detecting physical changes|A device that detects a physical condition and produces a signal or response.|cảm biến|A sensor switches on the corridor lights when someone enters.|Một cảm biến bật đèn hành lang khi có người đi vào.|Countable; common combinations include heat sensor and motion sensor.|sensor
route|travel-path|NOUN|Way between places|A path or course followed to travel from one place to another.|tuyến đường, lộ trình|The cyclists chose a route along the canal.|Những người đi xe đạp chọn một tuyến đường dọc theo kênh.|Countable; a route to a destination or a route through an area.|route
shopping|buying-activity|NOUN|Activity of buying goods|The activity of visiting shops or using services to buy goods.|việc mua sắm|We postponed our shopping until the rain stopped.|Chúng tôi hoãn việc mua sắm cho đến khi mưa tạnh.|Usually uncountable; go shopping and do the shopping are common patterns.|shopping
disgusting|causing-revulsion|ADJECTIVE|Causing strong dislike|So unpleasant that it makes someone feel revulsion or strong dislike.|ghê tởm, gớm ghiếc|A disgusting smell came from the blocked drain.|Một mùi ghê tởm bốc lên từ cống bị tắc.|Describes the cause of disgust; disgusted describes the person's reaction.|disgusting
environment|natural-world|NOUN|Natural surroundings|The natural world of land, water, air, and living things.|môi trường tự nhiên|The report describes how plastic waste harms the environment.|Báo cáo mô tả cách rác nhựa gây hại cho môi trường tự nhiên.|Usually the environment in this Sense; distinct from a particular social setting.|environment
environment|surrounding-conditions|NOUN|Conditions surrounding activity|The conditions and surroundings in which someone lives, works, or develops.|môi trường, điều kiện xung quanh nơi sống hoặc làm việc|The bright workshop provides a comfortable environment for learning.|Xưởng sáng sủa tạo một môi trường thoải mái cho việc học.|Countable for a particular setting; an environment for an activity.|environment
bedroom|sleeping-room|NOUN|Room for sleeping|A room in a home that is intended for sleeping.|phòng ngủ|They painted the bedroom walls pale blue.|Họ sơn tường phòng ngủ màu xanh lam nhạt.|Countable; bedroom describes the room's usual purpose.|bedroom
breeze|light-wind|NOUN|Gentle wind|A gentle movement of air outdoors.|làn gió nhẹ|A cool breeze stirred the curtains beside the open window.|Một làn gió mát nhẹ làm lay động rèm bên cửa sổ mở.|Countable; this Sense refers to wind, not something easy to do.|breeze
regular|repeated-intervals|ADJECTIVE|Repeated at steady intervals|Happening repeatedly with reasonably consistent intervals between occasions.|đều đặn|Regular visits kept the old friends in touch.|Những chuyến thăm đều đặn giúp những người bạn cũ giữ liên lạc.|Used for recurring activities; does not necessarily mean frequent or daily.|regular
